1.TWO SUM IN SORTED ARRAY
You are given a 1-based indexed integer array arr[] that is sorted in non-decreasing order, along with an integer target. 
Your task is to find two elements in the array such that their sum is equal to target. If such a pair exists, 
return the indices of the two elements in increasing order. If no such pair exists, return [-1, -1].
Note: If your answer is correct then the driver code will print "true" otherwise "false".
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public ArrayList<Integer> twoSum(int[] arr, int target) {
                Arrays.sort(arr);
                ArrayList<Integer> list=new ArrayList<>();
                int n=arr.length;
                int start=0;
                int end=n-1;
                while(start<end){
                    if(arr[start]+arr[end]==target){
                        list.add(start+1);
                        list.add(end+1);
                        return list;
                    }
                    else if(arr[start]+arr[end]>target){
                        end--;
                    }
                    else{
                        start++;
                    }
                }
                list.add(-1);
                list.add(-1);
                return list;
            }
        }
